import{_ as o,o as t,c as r,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"ADR-094 — Server-side observability for lab-api and mcp (errors, traces, metrics, access logs, analytics, LLM)","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"adr/ADR-094.md","filePath":"adr/ADR-094.md"}'),a={name:"adr/ADR-094.md"};function c(i,e,d,n,l,h){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="adr-094-—-server-side-observability-for-lab-api-and-mcp-errors-traces-metrics-access-logs-analytics-llm" tabindex="-1">ADR-094 — Server-side observability for lab-api and mcp (errors, traces, metrics, access logs, analytics, LLM) <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-094-—-server-side-observability-for-lab-api-and-mcp-errors-traces-metrics-access-logs-analytics-llm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ADR-094 — Server-side observability for lab-api and mcp (errors, traces, metrics, access logs, analytics, LLM)&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Status · Accepted · 2026-10-16 · Operator-directed (&quot;add all o11y elements to lab-api and mcp&quot;) · amends the OTLP non-goal in <strong>RFC-025</strong> and the errors-only scope of <strong>ADR-067</strong> for the two server processes only (the browser stays errors-only) · builds on <strong>ADR-081</strong> (Umami) and <strong>ADR-082</strong> (telemetry env ladder)</p></blockquote><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>RFC-025 ruled out OTLP traces because Orrery had &quot;no traceable workload (static SPA, no server)&quot;. It said to revisit &quot;when the VPS adds… a daemon&quot;. It now has two: <code>orrery-lab-api</code> (OAuth AS + <code>/ask</code> over the LiteLLM gateway) and <code>orrery-mcp</code> (64 physics tools over MCP). On 2026-10-16 their whole signal was one startup log line each:</p><ul><li>no error tracking (there was no server-side Sentry);</li><li>no traces (VictoriaTraces had no <code>orrery-*</code> services);</li><li>no request metrics;</li><li>no per-request log line;</li><li>no record of which MCP tools are used;</li><li><code>/ask</code>&#39;s LLM calls reached Langfuse with nothing to join them to a request.</li></ul><p>The podcast services on the same VPS already ship all six, and the homelab stack (VictoriaLogs/Metrics/Traces, GlitchTip, Umami, Langfuse) is the shared sink.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Both servers get the same six signals, modelled on podcast&#39;s player-api / player-mcp, all <strong>off unless configured</strong>. With every variable unset, nothing initialises and nothing leaves the process. That keeps tests, CI image smoke tests and forks silent.</p><ol><li><strong>Errors → GlitchTip</strong> via <code>@sentry/node</code>. Projects 31 <code>orrery-lab-api</code> and 32 <code>orrery-mcp</code>; DSNs are deploy secrets. Errors only: <code>tracesSampleRate</code> unset and Sentry&#39;s own OTel setup skipped, so it doesn&#39;t fight the tracer in (2). <code>environment</code> = <code>prod</code>, <code>release</code> = <code>sha-&lt;7&gt;</code> (homelab ADR-0010; the browser&#39;s <code>gha-&lt;8&gt;</code> is left as is). PII: no user email, no request bodies, no prompt text.</li><li><strong>Traces → VictoriaTraces</strong>, OTLP http/protobuf to <code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT</code>. The tracer is set up manually: the servers ship as one esbuild bundle with no <code>node_modules</code>, so require-hook auto-instrumentation is not available. <ul><li>Resource: <code>service.name</code> = <code>orrery-lab-api</code> | <code>orrery-mcp</code> (the same value as the logs&#39; <code>service</code> label), <code>deployment.environment</code> = <code>prod</code>, <code>service.version</code> = <code>sha-&lt;7&gt;</code>.</li><li>Spans: one server span per request (inbound <code>traceparent</code> honoured), one span per LLM call, one span per MCP / <code>/ask</code> tool call.</li><li><code>/health</code> and <code>/metrics</code> are never traced.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Metrics → VictoriaMetrics</strong> via <code>prom-client</code>, served on a separate internal port (<code>METRICS_PORT</code>, not published to the host, so never reachable through Caddy). <ul><li>Request count and latency by route and status.</li><li>For mcp, <code>mcp_tool_calls_total{tool,outcome}</code> and <code>mcp_tool_duration_seconds{tool}</code>; <code>tool</code> is bounded by the registry.</li><li>Scraped by the VPS Alloy from <code>orrery.alloy</code>, using the Docker-discovery → bridge-IP pattern <code>base.alloy</code> uses for the podcast APIs.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Access logs</strong>: one line per request: <code>METHOD route -&gt; status in N.Nms trace_id=&lt;32hex&gt;</code>. Alloy&#39;s existing trace-id stage turns it into a link from a log line to its trace. <code>/health</code> and <code>/metrics</code> are not logged.</li><li><strong>Analytics → Umami</strong>: mcp sends one server-side event per tool call to the Orrery site (hostname <code>mcp.orrerylearn.com</code>) with <code>{tool, outcome}</code>. It never carries user ids, arguments or prompt text.</li><li><strong>LLM → Langfuse via LiteLLM metadata</strong>: <code>/ask</code> sends <code>metadata</code> with: <ul><li><code>trace_id</code> = the OTel trace id;</li><li><code>trace_name</code> <code>orrery ask</code>;</li><li><code>session_id</code> = a per-request id (not a user id);</li><li><code>generation_name</code> = the tool round;</li><li><code>trace_release</code> = <code>sha-&lt;7&gt;</code>.</li></ul></li></ol><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>New runtime dependencies: <code>@sentry/node</code> (pinned to the same version as the rest of <code>@sentry/*</code>, which <code>@sentry/capacitor</code> enforces), <code>@opentelemetry/{api,sdk-trace-base,exporter-trace-otlp-proto,resources,semantic-conventions,core}</code> (on the line already installed), and <code>prom-client</code>.</li><li>Deploy: new GH <code>prod</code> secrets for the two DSNs. The OTLP endpoint and Umami site id are non-secret. Each value has to be added in three places (secret env, <code>.env</code> printf, compose <code>environment:</code>).</li><li>Scrape order: deploy the images first, then the <code>orrery.alloy</code> scrape, or <code>up</code> reads 0 until the new images serve <code>/metrics</code>. This is the podcast lesson recorded in <code>base.alloy</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="alternatives-considered" tabindex="-1">Alternatives considered <a class="header-anchor" href="#alternatives-considered" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Alternatives considered&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Auto-instrumentation</strong> (<code>@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node</code>): needs unbundled <code>node_modules</code> and require hooks. Rejected for the single-file images.</li><li><strong>Sentry tracing</strong> instead of OTel: it would send traces to GlitchTip, not VictoriaTraces, so they wouldn&#39;t join with logs and metrics.</li><li><strong><code>/metrics</code> on the public port, blocked at Caddy</strong>: one Caddyfile mistake away from public. Rejected for the separate internal port.</li></ul>',13)])])}const m=o(a,[["render",c]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
